%description:
Tests synRetries. The client sends its SYN again at most twice (12 times by
default), with an initial RTO of 1 s. The tester removes each SYN, so the SYNs
go at 0, 1 and 3 s, and at the third timeout (t=7) the open fails.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_tcp.initialRto = 1s
*.cli_tcp.synRetries = 2
*.tcptester.script="a1 delete; a2 delete; a3 delete"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[0.001 A001] A.1000 > B.2000: S 0:0(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize# deleting
[1.001 A002] A.1000 > B.2000: S 0:0(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize# deleting
[3.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: S 0:0(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize# deleting
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
Retransmission count during connection setup exceeds 2, giving up
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
